request:
MP3 export. A 6-min stereo mix at 320 takes ~14 s on my M1 and the UI stutters the whole time: progress bar jumps, meters freeze, and Cancel takes a second or two to register. Two Discord reports this week, one from a guy exporting 40-min DJ sets where it's over a minute of frozen app. Options:

A. Keep `@breezystack/lamejs`, move `audioBufferToMp3` into a worker. The writer route already streams packets to the file, so mostly plumbing: transfer PCM blocks in, post packets out.
B. WebCodecs `AudioEncoder`. Platform encoder, native code, runs off the main thread by design, and it drops the LGPL dependency.
C. Build LAME 3.100 to wasm with emscripten, SIMD on, in a worker.

Leaning B, and here's my reasoning so you can poke holes:

1. A fixes the jank but not the speed. lamejs is a straight JS port of LAME from 2015, it's ~6-8x slower than native LAME. In a worker the 40-min set still takes 90+ s, just without freezing.
2. B is native speed and we're Chromium-only (web + Electron 44), so there's no "Safari doesn't have it" problem.
3. MP3 is the easy WebCodecs case: MP3 frames are self-contained, so `EncodedAudioChunk` bytes can go straight into the file. No muxer, unlike AAC which needs an MP4 container (that's why the m4a ticket is bigger).
4. It retires `test:lgpl-runtime` for lamejs. That gate also covers Electron's libffmpeg so it doesn't disappear entirely, but the lamejs half is the part that breaks on every lamejs bump because the provenance archive has to be re-fetched and restamped.
5. C is the "real" fix for speed but it's an emscripten toolchain in CI, LGPL still applies, and we'd own a LAME build forever.

Current encoder, `AudioRendering/repositories/audioEncoders/mp3Encoder.ts`:

```ts
import { Mp3Encoder } from '@breezystack/lamejs';
...
export async function audioBufferToMp3(buffer, bitRate = 128, onProgress, dither, writer) {
    const numChannels = Math.min(buffer.numberOfChannels, 2);
    const encoder = new Mp3Encoder(numChannels, buffer.sampleRate, bitRate);
    const pcm = createPcmBlockReader({ source: buffer, bitDepth: 16, dither, channelLimit: 2 });
    ...
    for (let start = 0; start < buffer.length; start += 1152) {
        destination.checkCancelled?.();
        const block = pcm.read(1152);
        const left = Int16Array.from(block.channels[0]!);
        const right = numChannels === 2 ? Int16Array.from(block.channels[1]!) : undefined;
        const packet = encoder.encodeBuffer(left, right);
        if (packet.length > 0) {
            await destination.write(packet);
        }
        onProgress?.((start + block.length) / Math.max(1, buffer.length));
        if ((start + block.length) % (1152 * 64) === 0) {
            await new Promise<void>((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 0));
        }
    }
    ...
}
```

